========================================================================
4. Outside material
========================================================================

  - Third-party payload text, original or adapted, stays under its
    source's MIT license wherever it appears. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
    carries the notices, and corpus/release/payloads.json records each
    entry's source. The license notices that file quotes belong to
    their sources.
  - No license is claimed over model-generated text in released
    records. The provider's terms haven't been verified.
  - Third-party packages, which uv.lock lists, keep their own licenses.
  - This file covers only what is in the public repository. Raw records
    and restricted audit material stay outside Git, and
    docs/DATA_RELEASE.md decides what ships.

